  contentId: phy_gravity_01
  subject: Physics
  title: Gravity
  notes: "Gravity is the force of attraction between any two objects in the universe,
    and it is responsible for objects falling to the Earth and for the motion of
    planets and moons in their orbits. Centripetal force is the inward force that
    keeps a body moving in a circular path, such as the moon orbiting the Earth due
    to the Earth\u2019s gravitational pull."
